{"result":[{"biographic_references":[],"contributors":{"authors":[{"aliases":[],"checked":"1","codes":["radin.charles"],"name":"Radin, Charles"}],"author_references":[],"editors":[]},"database":"Zbl","datestamp":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","document_type":{"code":"j","description":"journal article"},"editorial_contributions":[{"language":"English","reviewer":{"author_code":null,"reviewer_id":null,"name":null,"sign":"N.Arley"},"text":"The author gives a purely mathematical treatment of the problem of spatial symmetry in low-temperature crystals where the energy ground states tend to be periodic. The author states to have essentially solved the problem for one-dimensional models in previous papers. \n\n\nIn this paper the problem is treated for two- and three-dimensional models. It is shown that energy ground states here tend to have a homogeneity property at least in an average sense, whereby ``homogeneous'' is taken to mean that the configuration is essentially identical (statistically) in any two congruent regions much larger than the period. No physical or technical applications are given.","contribution_type":"review"}],"id":4028595,"identifier":"0632.60109","keywords":[],"language":{"languages":["English"],"addition":[null]},"license":[],"links":[{"identifier":"10.1007/BF01020661","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01020661"}],"msc":[{"code":"60K35","scheme":"msc2020","text":"Interacting random processes; statistical mechanics type models; percolation theory"},{"code":"82B05","scheme":"msc2020","text":"Classical equilibrium statistical mechanics (general)"}],"references":[{"doi":null,"position":"1","text":"B. Simon,Perspectives in Mathematics: Anniversary of Oberwolfach 1985 (Birkhauser Verlag, Basel, 1984), p. 442.","zbmath":{"author_codes":[],"document_id":null,"msc":[],"prefix":null,"series_id":0,"year":null}},{"doi":null,"position":"2","text":"S. G. Brush,Statistical Physics and the Atomic Theory of Matter (Princeton University Press, Princeton, 1983),